  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kentucky has received $8.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 18.9% year over year while agencies awarded 81,644 contracts with an average award size of $104K. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $7.7B, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $5.6B. HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC is the largest vendor in the state with $5.6B in obligations, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION with $584M. Annual trends show a peak near $12.5B in FY23 and a decline to $10.4B in FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $8.5B. The Top 10 buying agencies list includes the Department of the Treasury at $205M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $158M. The Top 10 industries list includes All Other Support Services at $589M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $370M. This summary highlights who bought what and which firms captured the most federal obligations in Kentucky so far in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Kentucky trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 18.9% year over year from the prior fiscal period. Obligations by fiscal year peaked at $12.5B in FY23 then moved to $12.3B in FY24 and $10.4B in FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $8.5B. The number of awards in FY2026 to date is 81,644 with an average award size of $104K. These figures show the current fiscal year to date totals are partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and vendors in Kentucky federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $7.7B in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $205M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $158M. HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC is the largest vendor with $5.6B, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION with $584M and THALLE - BAUER LLC with $345M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $5.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Kentucky?",
      "a": "Kentucky received $8.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations by fiscal year were $11.8B in FY21, $11.9B in FY22, $12.5B in FY23, $12.3B in FY24, $10.4B in FY25, and $8.5B in FY26. The FY2026 to date total reflects partial current-year obligations."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Kentucky?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Kentucky with $7.7B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other top buying agencies include the Department of the Treasury with $205M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $158M. The Top 10 buyers list also includes the Department of Justice at $156M and the Department of Homeland Security at $72.4M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Kentucky?",
      "a": "HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC is the largest federal contractor in Kentucky with $5.6B in obligations in FY2026 to date. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the second largest with $584M and THALLE - BAUER LLC is third with $345M. Other top vendors include WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $188M and BAE SYSTEMS LAND & ARMAMENTS L.P. at $145M."
    }
